From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:15:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cli: join topology to authoritative radio inventory

The get_network topology projection does not place a direct RadioList below
the Controller and colocated-Agent records.  A recursive RadioList lookup then
falls into the first descendant and renders that extender's BSSs on several
unrelated nodes.  This makes topology BSSID/name resolution unsafe after a
steer even though the flat controller model remains correct.

Read the authoritative get_sta DeviceList once, copy each Agent's RadioList
into Go-owned values, and join it to topology records by exact AL MAC.  Use the
same inventory for the devices endpoint and backhaul-band rendering.  A node
with no matching Agent record now has no invented radios.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/rdkb-cli/main.go | 72 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 67 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
--- a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
+++ b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
@@ -3196,5 +3196,47 @@ func controllerIPHandler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
 
 }
+
+// loadLiveRadioInventory copies the flat controller Agent inventory into Go
+// values. get_network is a topology projection and its nested child records
+// do not consistently contain their own RadioList.
+func loadLiveRadioInventory() (map[string][]Radio, error) {
+    cmd := C.CString("get_sta OneWifiMesh")
+    defer C.free(unsafe.Pointer(cmd))
+
+    var tree *C.em_network_node_t
+    for attempt := 0; attempt < 3; attempt++ {
+        tree = execEMCommand(cmd, nil)
+        if tree != nil {
+            break
+        }
+        time.Sleep(200 * time.Millisecond)
+    }
+    if tree == nil {
+        return nil, fmt.Errorf("controller returned no radio inventory data")
+    }
+    defer C.free_network_tree(tree)
+
+    deviceList := getNetworkTreeByKey(tree, "DeviceList")
+    if deviceList == nil {
+        return nil, fmt.Errorf("controller radio inventory has no DeviceList")
+    }
+
+    inventory := make(map[string][]Radio)
+    for index := 0; index < int(deviceList.num_children); index++ {
+        device := deviceList.child[index]
+        if device == nil {
+            continue
+        }
+        deviceID := strings.ToLower(getTreeValue(device, "ID"))
+        radioList := getNetworkTreeByKey(device, "RadioList")
+        if deviceID == "" || radioList == nil {
+            continue
+        }
+        inventory[deviceID] = parseRadioList(radioList)
+    }
+    return inventory, nil
+}
+
